      "boundaryDescription": "PART 1 Greater High Cross Area: \"The area bounded by Adelaide Terrace to the north; St Johns Road to the east; Atkinson Road to the west; and Armstrong Road to the south and the area bounded by Armstrong Road to the north, east by Atkinson Road; South Benwell Road to the west; and Whitehouse Road to the south.\" PART 2 Byker Old Town Area: \"The area within Byker Old Town bounded by Welbeck Road to the south, Roman Avenue to the east Grace Street to the north and Bothal Street to the west.\" PART 3 Byker Allendale South: \"The area of Allendale South consisting of 63-189 Allendale Road, 1-7 Bird Nest Road, Chatsworth Gardens, Irthing Avenue and Relton Avenue.\"",
      "evidence": "This is The Newcastle City Council Designation of an Area for Selective Licensing Greater High Cross and Byker 2021, enclosed with the council's landlord letter of 30 June 2021, and it is still the only Byker/High Cross designation in force today. The designation defines Part 1 (Greater High Cross) and Part 2 (Byker Old Town) ONLY by a worded boundary, not by a street list, so no street list can honestly be given for those two parts; the five streets listed here are Part 3 (Byker Allendale South), which the designation does enumerate verbatim. Numbers are transcribed exactly as written (63-189 Allendale Road, 1-7 Bird Nest Road) and the designation says 'Bird Nest Road' singular, whereas the 2026 renewal spells it 'Birds Nest Road'. Do NOT borrow the 2026 renewal street list for this scheme: the areas differ, e.g. 2021 Allendale Road is 63-189 whereas the 2026 renewal is 31-189 odds."
