      "evidence": "Transcribed verbatim from The Newcastle City Council Designation of an Area for Selective Licensing 2025 (made 22 October 2024), Parts 1-6: Cowgate, HHRS, West End, Columbia Grange, Denton Court and Lemington. The designation defines the area purely by named streets with number restrictions, so there is no worded boundary. Cross-checked with two extraction modes (pdftotext -layout and PyMuPDF) plus pdfplumber word coordinates; the only disagreement was around Parts 4 and 5, where pdftotext -layout floated the number ranges out of reading order, and coordinate analysis confirms Columbia Grange = '1-20 all numbers' and Denton Court = '1-24 all numbers'. This scheme replaced the earlier 6 April 2020 five-area scheme (Cowgate, East End, HHRS, Scotswood Village, West End), whose East End and Scotswood Village areas were NOT renewed and are no longer licensable."
