      "evidence": "Transcribed from the designation document (Parts 1-2, tabulated as Street Name / numbers / All-or-Part) and cross-checked line by line against the separate Public Notice of Designation dated 24 February 2026, which repeats the same list as running text. The two disagree in three places and the designation instrument has been preferred: it gives 'Brook Street 70-74 evens, 71-76 odds' where the notice reads '70-74 odds and 71-76 odds'; 'Hodgkin Park Crescent' where the notice reads 'Hodgin Park Crescent'; and 'Scarborough Court' where the notice reads 'Scarbrough Court'. The designation abbreviates 'Roman Ave' and 'Tunstall Ave'; the notice spells both out and those full forms are used here. Atherton Drive is whole-street ('All numbers including Manisty House') so numbers is null. This scheme takes over from the 2021 Byker/High Cross designation and its area is NOT identical to it (Allendale Road becomes 31-189 odds, up from 63-189), so do not apply this list before 30 September 2026. The council's Selective Licensing web page says the scheme starts '1 October 2026'; the legal instrument and public notice both say 30 September 2026, and the legal date is used here."
